00:00:05.030 --> 00:00:07.730 align:start position:0%
what is the euro area also known as the  euro zone it is made up of the EU member  states that have adopted the euro as  their currency the euro was first  introduced in 1999 as an accounting  currency banknotes and coins followed in  2002 the euro is now the currency of  over three hundred and thirty seven  million EU citizens it is also a major  trading currency outside the EU most EU  member states are in the euro area the  UK and Denmark have opted out while  others have yet to fulfill conditions  for entry to join the Euro countries  have to meet economic and legal  conditions known as the Maastricht  convergence criteria only then will the  Commission the Parliament and the  central bank consider a country's  request to join the euro area the  council must take the final decision  through a vote ministers from the euro  area member states work together in an  informal body called the Euro group the  Euro group is chaired by a president  elected by its members for two and a  half years the president also represents  the euro area at international level the  Euro group ensures that euro area  countries closely coordinate their  economic and budgetary policies it also  prepares the euro summit meetings that  bring together heads of state or  government of the euro area countries  they provide strategic guidelines for  euro area economic policy find out all  you want to know about the euro area and  much more on Concilium euro / Ian  [Music]
 

